+# Shipment Invoice create UI — FRO-363
+
+Approved layout A implemented with portal components and TanStack Form. This feature is intentionally **unmounted**. There is no production route, backend adapter, authority definition, API/schema change, or persistent mock service.
+
+## Integration boundary
+
+Import ShipmentInvoiceCreateForm from ../components/shipment-invoice-create-form. Its props are presentation interfaces, not backend schemas. The host supplies authorized Shipment candidates, current eligible rows and reasons, currencies, authoritative evaluated totals/currency conflicts/overlap references, and draft submission. No allocation, money/rounding or exchange-rate algorithm lives here.
+
+- todayAthens must be a YYYY-MM-DD calendar date in Europe/Athens. Do not derive it by slicing UTC ISO time. The portal DatePicker displays dd-mm-yyyy here.
+- initialShipmentId is fixed for one mounted form instance. Remount when changing entry context. User-driven Shipment changes are confirmed in the form.
+- registerNavigationGuard installs the provided callback into the host router/navigation blocker and returns cleanup. Call the callback with a continuation for every internal navigation attempt, including browser Back. Dirty navigation opens confirmation; pending save blocks navigation; successful-save navigation is explicitly allowed. This integration is required before activation. beforeunload protects reload/close independently.
+- onSaved receives the persisted identity and must navigate to the real Details UI. A thrown navigation failure preserves identity and offers retry without another submit.
+- onCancel navigates to originating Shipment, else the previous page with Shipments fallback. The form confirms dirty cancellation before calling it.
+- onOpenAllocation opens the authorized Order allocation UI in a new tab. No route is guessed. Missing callback is visibly unavailable. Refresh is explicit and never writes allocation.
+- available and missing callback handling express host-provided availability only. They are not authorization. FRO-244 must enforce backend access and validation.
+- Async reads/evaluations are generation-guarded. Failed eligibility reads keep work visible but block selection and saving until successful refresh.
+- FRO-244 owns persistence, eligibility, current values, totals and overlap information. FRO-301 owns allocation. Saved Details and allocation UI routes remain delivery dependencies.
+
+## Components and appearance
+
+Uses Card/CardHeader/CardTitle/CardBody; Input/Textarea/FormField; Select; DatePicker; Checkbox; Table primitives; Modal; Alert; Button. Sources are components/ui/\*.tsx, components/form/index.ts and app/providers/labels-provider.tsx. Layout uses existing semantic tokens from styles/theme.css. The containing app owns AppShell, sidebar and topbar; this form does not duplicate navigation.
+
+The Shipment picker composes a search input, Search action and existing Select for returned candidates. The shared Combobox did not commit keyboard choices in local verification; Select preserves keyboard operation without changing the shared primitive. DatePicker is used directly within the form because its format prop supports the approved dd-mm-yyyy requirement, unlike the current DateField wrapper. All values still live in TanStack Form.
+
+Grouped goods selection and totals are new compositions, not new primitives. Unresolved rows are disabled separately. Source identity and group order are retained. HS codes remain text. Totals are supplied by the host, not calculated in UI helpers.
+
+## Local verification
+
+Use Node 22.13.0 and pnpm 11.1.3 with pnpm install --frozen-lockfile, matching the client Dockerfile. No dependency changes required.
+
+- npm test -- src/features/shipment-invoices
+- npm run test
+- npm run build
+- npm run format:check
+- pnpm exec tsc --noEmit
+
+A temporary local Vite host mounts this form with the existing LabelsProvider and ThemeProvider (compact), importing styles/theme.css. Tailwind must include an explicit @source for src when the harness root is outside the usual app root. The host injects fixtures from **fixtures**/shipment-invoice-create.ts. Fixtures are not imported by operational components. A Playwright review exercises EN/EL at 1440px and 400px, read states, failure states and consequential form flows. The temporary host is not in the proposed diff.
+
+The review only proves frontend behavior. Activation requires real adapters, authority checks, pagination/lookup contract, currency reference data, Details/allocation navigation and router leave-blocking. No production calls were made. Full verification evidence is recorded in the planning repository's FRO-363 handoff report.
